    "id": "e6d16bf79b30695420d3ac3a",
    "path": "datafusion_pruning::file_pruner::FilePruner::try_new",
    "name": "try_new",
    "owner": "datafusion_pruning::file_pruner::FilePruner",
    "crate": "datafusion-pruning",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "function",
    "signature": "fn try_new(predicate: Arc<dyn PhysicalExpr>, file_schema: &SchemaRef, partitioned_file: &PartitionedFile, predicate_creation_errors: Count) -> Option<Self>",
    "docs": "Create a file pruner for this file, or `None` when pruning it cannot\nhelp.\n\nReturns `None` when the file has no statistics struct to evaluate a\npruning predicate against, or when the predicate is purely static and the\nfile has no usable column statistics — in that case planning already did\neverything such a pruner could. A predicate carrying a dynamic filter is\nalways accepted (given a statistics struct), since it may prune via\npartition-value folding even without column statistics.",
